{#-
  HeroMedia — a poster that paints immediately with a silent, looping video
  that fades in over it once it is genuinely playing.

  The poster is the LCP element, so it is a real <picture> with
  fetchpriority="high"; the <video> carries no sources and no autoplay
  attribute. site.js attaches after load, picks the cut that matches the
  shape of the box, and calls play(). If anything says no — reduced motion,
  Save-Data, a rejected play(), a decode error — the poster simply stays and
  the page is a photograph, which is a perfectly good outcome.

  Parameters (all optional except alt):
    base    directory holding the files        default /assets/video/hero
    name    file-name stem                     default hero
    alt     poster alt text, already localised  REQUIRED
    class   extra class on the wrapper

  Choosing the crop: the hero fills the viewport, so the box IS the viewport
  and the crop can be switched on the viewport's own aspect ratio. That is
  what makes poster and video agree by construction rather than by estimate:
  both read the same number, and no window height can put them out of step.

    < 0.68        9:16 cut  -> mobile poster   (phones held upright)
    0.68 - 1.20   4:5 cut   -> panel poster    (tablets upright, square-ish)
    > 1.20        16:9 cut  -> desktop poster  (laptops, tablets on their side)

  The two boundaries are repeated in three places and must stay in step: the
  media queries below, cutFor() in site.js, and the preload hints in base.njk.
-#}
{%- macro heroMedia(opts) -%}
{%- set base = opts.base | default('/assets/video/hero') -%}
{%- set name = opts.name | default('hero') -%}
<div class="hero-media hero-media--video{{ ' ' ~ opts.class if opts.class }}"
     data-hero-media
     data-base="{{ base }}"
     data-name="{{ name }}">
  {#- First match wins, so these run narrowest first and the last pair is the
      catch-all for everything wider than 1.20. -#}
  <picture class="hero-media__poster">
    <source media="(max-aspect-ratio:68/100)" srcset="{{ base }}/{{ name }}-poster-mobile.webp" type="image/webp">
    <source media="(max-aspect-ratio:68/100)" srcset="{{ base }}/{{ name }}-poster-mobile.jpg">
    <source media="(max-aspect-ratio:120/100)" srcset="{{ base }}/{{ name }}-poster-panel.webp" type="image/webp">
    <source media="(max-aspect-ratio:120/100)" srcset="{{ base }}/{{ name }}-poster-panel.jpg">
    <source srcset="{{ base }}/{{ name }}-poster-desktop.webp" type="image/webp">
    <img src="{{ base }}/{{ name }}-poster-desktop.jpg"
         alt="{{ opts.alt }}"
         width="1920" height="1080"
         fetchpriority="high" decoding="async">
  </picture>
  {#- No src, no autoplay: the script owns loading so the poster never
      competes with it for bandwidth. aria-hidden because the poster's alt
      already describes the content; the video adds nothing for a screen
      reader and is purely decorative. -#}
  <video class="hero-media__video" muted loop playsinline
         preload="none" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></video>
</div>
{%- endmacro -%}
